Continuation rubric
- P1 preserved: pass. Both target Inputs resolve to the same local target class and exact computed geometry/treatment (320x36, padding-inline 18px, gap 10px, radius 6px, rgb(243,247,252)).
- P2 preserved: pass. Both current-feature Buttons are primary; the non-target Button remains secondary with frozen computed style.
- Reuse rather than copied declarations: pass. Both states reference native-baseline__target-input; no second-state copy of its CSS declarations exists.
- Local Input Part: pass. Only the second state contains a direct child [data-slot="scope-label"] with stable ID native-baseline-second-scope-label.
- Accessible relation: pass. The second input references the scope-label through aria-describedby and exposes the accessible description "课程范围".
- Global/non-target absence: pass. The first shared Input and non-target shared Input contain no scope-label part.
- Master/Foundation/icon/package/route/global CSS protection: pass by exact hashes and browser assertions.
- Formal SearchIcon: pass. Both states use @rain-next/ui/icons/search; manifest availability, one export/import identity, Figma node 8:20, mask rendering, 16x16 sizing, and decorative accessibility remain asserted.
- Keyboard continuation: pass. Tab from the second Input reaches its paired Button.
